{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/why-your-phone-battery-gets-low/audio/main-66dfa3b28cbf.mp3","durationSec":69,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.2,"text":"Many modern phones use a rechargeable lithium-ion battery."},{"start":3.8,"end":5.92,"text":"It stores energy for the phone."},{"start":6.86,"end":10.38,"text":"Each time you charge and use the battery, it changes a little."},{"start":11.02,"end":14.22,"text":"After many months or years, it cannot hold as much energy as before."},{"start":15.04,"end":17.64,"text":"Apple calls this chemical ageing."},{"start":17.64,"end":19.28,"text":"It is a normal part of battery life."},{"start":19.96,"end":21.54,"text":"Heat is hard on a phone battery."},{"start":22.1,"end":25.92,"text":"A hot battery can lose power quickly, and heat can make it age faster."},{"start":26.38,"end":29.26,"text":"Do not leave your phone in a hot car or in strong sun."},{"start":30.2,"end":33.34,"text":"If the phone gets very hot, move it to a cooler place and let it cool."},{"start":34.22,"end":36.48,"text":"The screen and busy apps can use a lot of energy."},{"start":37.02,"end":38.56,"text":"A bright screen needs more power."},{"start":39.06,"end":41.56,"text":"Video, maps, and games can also use power quickly."},{"start":42.56,"end":45.02,"text":"Lower the screen brightness and let the screen turn off sooner."},{"start":45.82,"end":48.64,"text":"Your battery settings can show which apps use the most power."},{"start":49.24,"end":51.56,"text":"You can charge your phone when you need to."},{"start":51.86,"end":57.94,"text":"You do not have to wait until the battery is at zero, and you do not have to charge it to 100 percent every time."},{"start":58.84,"end":63.52,"text":"Use the charger made for your phone or another charger that the maker says is safe to use."},{"start":64.32,"end":68.6,"text":"When you need more time, turn on Battery Saver or Low Power Mode."}],"words":[{"text":"Many","start":0,"end":0.32